\description{
Tiger mosquito egg counts from an ovitrap network in six towns around the
border between Ticino and Lombardy, used to ask whether the integrated
vector management (IVM) programme run on the Swiss side actually suppresses
the mosquito. The three Ticino municipalities (Balerna, Coldrerio,
Mendrisio) have followed the cantonal IVM since 2009; the three Italian ones
(Malnate, Maslianico, Uggiate-Trevano), a few kilometres away and comparable
in climate, altitude and urban structure, have no coordinated programme and
serve as the control. Six sites per town, one ovitrap per site, read roughly
every fortnight from late May to October 2019.
}
